# React Web Design Quality

## Product-specific UI
- Do not ship generic template-looking UI; make surfaces specific to the product, workflow, and audience.
- Apps, tools, and games start with the actual usable experience, not a default marketing page.
- Choose a concrete style direction before coding and express it through tokens, layout, typography, states, and motion.
- Finish hover, focus, active, loading, empty, and error states intentionally.

## Required qualities
- Clear hierarchy through scale, density, and spacing contrast.
- Intentional rhythm instead of uniform padding everywhere.
- Depth/layering only when it improves comprehension.
- Deliberate typography and semantic color.
- Data visualizations treated as part of the design system.
- Motion that clarifies state changes and respects reduced motion.

## Must not do
- No decorative card grids, generic hero sections, or workflow-free dashboards.
- No hardcoded colors, spacing, font sizes, radii, or shadows; extend shared design tokens first.
- No page sections inside floating cards.
- No color-only state or flourishes that hide real product state.

## Verification
- Check desktop/mobile overflow, text clipping, overlap, and visible focus states.
- Use Playwright screenshots for visual-heavy changes.
